<Style
  backgroundColor="#F7F6F9"
  backgroundYPadding="24"
  bodyColor="#FFFFFF"
  bodyXPadding="32"
  bodyYPadding="28"
  borderColor="#E6E4EC"
  borderWidth="1"
  borderRadius="16"
  textBaseColor="#3A4B52"
  textBaseFontSize="16"
  textBaseLineHeight="160"
  textLinkColor="#04576A"
  heading1Color="#17242B"
  heading1FontSize="23"
  heading1LineHeight="130"
  buttonBodyColor="#04576A"
  buttonTextColor="#FFFFFF"
  buttonBorderRadius="10"
  buttonBodyXPadding="28"
  buttonBodyYPadding="14"
  buttonTextFontSize="16"
  dividerColor="#E6E4EC"
  dividerBorderWidth="1"
/>

<Divider color="#04576A" borderWidth="6" paddingTop="0" paddingBottom="20" />

<Image src="LOOPS_HOSTED_LOGO_URL" alt="TimetoPay" width="44" align="left" borderRadius="10" paddingBottom="20" />

<H1 paddingBottom="14">Welcome to TimetoPay, {contact.firstName}</H1>

<Paragraph paddingBottom="16">You're set up. The quickest way to see what it does:</Paragraph>

<!-- One Paragraph per item rather than a single block split by <Br />. Two
     reasons: <Br /> gave no vertical gap so the three ran together as a wall of
     text, and the source indentation after each <Br /> leaked through as a
     visible leading space before "Build" and "Get". Separate blocks fix both,
     and paddingBottom controls the rhythm explicitly. -->
<Paragraph paddingBottom="10"><Strong>Scan a receipt.</Strong> We pull out every item and price for you.</Paragraph>

<Paragraph paddingBottom="10"><Strong>Build up your price history.</Strong> After a few receipts you'll see the best store and price for the things you buy often.</Paragraph>

<Paragraph paddingBottom="24"><Strong>Get a shopping list.</Strong> Built from what you actually buy.</Paragraph>

<Button href="https://5to9shopping.com/scan">Scan your first receipt</Button>

<Divider paddingTop="24" paddingBottom="16" />

<Paragraph fontSize="12" lineHeight="160"><Text textColor="#8FA3A0">Happy saving, the TimetoPay team</Text></Paragraph>
